                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          %p
            hence of the
            = succeed "-comonad" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mi Store
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S Store
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            as providing the computational context consisting of data base (of “stored
            = succeed "-values\u201D," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed ")" do
              %em store comonad
          %p
            Thus the
            = succeed "-operation" do
              %em obtain
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:InternalHomAdjunctionCoUnit"} (3)
            literally obtains (reads, extracts) the memory content at the given address.
          %h3#on_closed_monoidal_categories On closed monoidal categories
          %p
            More generally, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝟙
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes, \mathbb{1})
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal category
            (not necessarily
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            still still gives an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal-hom"} internal-hom
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjunction
            of the form
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CartesianInternalHomAdjunction"} (1)
          #eq:MonoidalInternalHomAdjunction.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %munderover
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⊥
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi S
                        %mo ,
                        %mtext -
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mtext -
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{C}
                  \\underoverset
                  {\underset{[S,\text{-}]}{\longrightarrow}}
                  {\overset{S \otimes (\text{-})}{\longleftarrow}}
                  {\;\; \bot \;\;}
                  \\mathcal{C}
          %p
            and the
            %a{:href => "monad#RelationBetweenAdjunctionsAndMonads"} induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            may be understood as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substructural+logic"} substructural
            forms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state+monad"} state monad
            and store comonad, respectively.
          %p
            Particularly when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ≡
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Mod
                    %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} \,\equiv\, Mod_{\mathbb{C}}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+vector+bundles"} category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+spaces"} complex vector spaces
            (“
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            \-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+spaces"}> linear spaces
            ”) this gives a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+type+theory"} linear
            form of the costate comonad, discussed at
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+costate+comonad"} quantum costate comonad
              \.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#realization_by_base_change Realization by base change
          %p
            In a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+Cartesian+closed+category"} locally Cartesian closed category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            is associated its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi W
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                            %mi W
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi W
                            %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mi W
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{H}_{/W}
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\sum_W}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{W^\ast}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{\prod_W}{\longrightarrow}}}
                  \\mathbf{H}
                  \\,.
          %p In terms of this the store comonad is the composite
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Store
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mi W
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mo *
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mi W
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Store = \sum_W W^\ast \prod_W W^\ast
          %p
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context+extension"} context extension
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
            , followed by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context+extension"} context extension
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mi W
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mo *
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi W
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_W W^\ast = [W,-]
            is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+monad"} function monad
            or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reader+monad"} reader monad
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mi W
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mo *
                  %mo =
                  %mi W
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_W W^\ast = W \times (-)
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/writer+comonad"} writer comonad
          %h3#LabelStoreComodulesAreLenses Store-Comodules are Lenses
          %p
            We spell out the data of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comodule+over+a+comonad"} comodules
            over the classical Store comonad defined
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#OnACartesianClosedCategory"} above
          %blockquote
            %p
              (Beware that we are switching from using “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              ” for the state space to using it for the argument of the comonad – this in order to be closer to the notation used at
              = succeed ".)" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lens+in+computer+science"} lens in computer science
          %p
            Unwinding the definitions, a
            = succeed "-store" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comodule+over+a+comonad"} comodule
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            on a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/map"} map
            of the form
          #eq:ComoduleMap.maruku-equation
