          %p
            This data — a pair of maps
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LensStructureMaps"} (6)
            satisfying the
            %em get-put law
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:GetPutLaw"} (7)
            %em put-get law
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PutGetLaw"} (8)
            and the
            %em put-put law
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PutPutLaw"} (9)
            – is known as a
            %em
              lawful
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lens+in+computer+science"} lens in computer science
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#lens+in+computer+science#Lens"} there
          %p
            Hence, as first observed by
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#O’Connor10"} O’Connor 2010
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Classical
              = succeed "-store" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
